DeepSeek Harness (dsh) is DeepSeek's open-source agent harness: a
"everything is a plugin" coding agent with a CLI, a browser web UI, and a
plugin/skill system.

This port packages the FreeBSD-maintained fork, which adds the FreeBSD-only
pieces the upstream release lacks:

- a native flock(2) addon for the JSONL session store,
- a FreeBSD process inspector and bash PTY fixes,
- a FreeBSD jail sandbox backend (setuid dsh-jail-run helper),
- ripgrep/bash path resolution and a loopback-only web trust fence.

Run `dsh web` for the web UI (loopback-only; reach it through an SSH
tunnel) or `service dsh_web start` for the boot-time service. See
pkg-message after install for the full quick start.
